From b0d6482f41608a356d962ce9df0260d28555aeb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] output: keep the working render format when every candidate
 fails

output_set_render_format() walks its candidate list and leaves whichever
it tried last on output->pending when none of them passes. From then on no
swapchain can be created for that output, and every frame fails with
"Failed to pick primary buffer format" - naming a colour format the
renderer never supported, which is a long way from whatever actually made
the probe fail.

Remember the format that was working before the probe started, and put it
back when the probe finds nothing.

Found while running labwc against a wlroots patched to hand a fullscreen
video's overlay surface to an output layer, which made a probe fail on a
box where one never had before. The bug is not layer-specific though: any
cause of a failed probe reaches it.
---
 src/output.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/output.c b/src/output.c
index 2eab8ec..f91e92d 100644
--- a/src/output.c
+++ b/src/output.c
@@ -87,12 +87,14 @@ uint32_t output_formats_10bit[] = {
 static bool
 output_set_render_format(struct output *output, uint32_t candidates[], size_t count)
 {
+	uint32_t working = output->wlr_output->render_format;
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
 		wlr_output_state_set_render_format(&output->pending, candidates[i]);
 		if (wlr_output_test_state(output->wlr_output, &output->pending)) {
 			return true;
 		}
 	}
+	wlr_output_state_set_render_format(&output->pending, working);
 	return false;
 }
 
